Method overriding

It can only be done when inheritance is performed
It is used to provide extraction
Method overriding happens when a child class defines a method with the same name as a method in its parent class, allowing the child class to provide its own implementation.


class A:
    def show(self):
        print("A")
class b(A):
    def show(self):
        print("B")
	A.show(self)  # to call the method of parent class
	self.display() # to call method from same class
    
      def display(self):
        print("class b")


obj= b()
obj.show()
